  "worked_solution": "We can form a triangle by creating a vertical line from $A$ to the $x$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14216822/assets/d4aa760fae46877c78d0bb2b87b7b047832a2600258401af1d021f693bb788b3.png)\n\nUsing the tangent ratio, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{1}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nUsing the inverse tangent, we get\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}={60}^{∘}.\n$$",
